From a1b9e263f7c55de8ff1d00fe1e5d0d846288d06c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:19:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix(tools): close read_url SSRF gaps (userinfo, IPv6,
 CGNAT, redirects)

isPrivateUrl took the host with a regex over the raw string, so
`http://user:pass@10.0.0.1/` was judged by "user" and fetched. It also missed
IPv6 private ranges, IPv4-mapped IPv6, 100.64.0.0/10 (CGNAT / Tailscale peers),
.local/.internal names, and anything reached through a redirect.

- Move the guard to tools/privateUrl.ts and read the host from the URL parser
  (react-native-url-polyfill is loaded in index.js), which also normalises
  shorthand IPv4 such as http://2130706433/.
- Block loopback, RFC 1918, link-local/metadata, CGNAT, multicast/reserved,
  ::, ::1, fc00::/7, fe80::/10, ::ffff:<private v4>, cloud metadata hosts,
  .localhost/.local/.internal/.lan/.home.arpa, single-label names, non-http(s)
  schemes and unparsable URLs.
- After fetch, refuse the body when response.url landed on a private address.

Based on fl4p/off-grid-ai-mobile 216c73494 (userinfo, CGNAT) and
longregen/off-grid-mobile-ai f417b1a8c (IPv6, metadata hosts, suffixes); the
redirect check is new.

